ate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.0030846799679784542,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":23.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.004657186558300941,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":44.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03450222822689601,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":42.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.081870005,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":54.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Tejon Ranch Co., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a diversified real estate development and agribusiness company. It operates through six segments: Real Estate - Commercial/Industrial; Multifamily; Real Estate - Resort/Residential; Mineral Resources; Farming; And Ranch Operations. The Real Estate - Commercial/Industrial segment engages in the planning and permitting of land for development; construction of infrastructure and building, pre-leased buildings, and buildings to be leased or sold; sale of land to third parties for their own development; and activities related to communications leases, a power plant lease, and landscape maintenance. This segment also leases land to various auto service stations with convenience stores, fast-food operations, a motel, an antique shop, and a post office; various microwave repeater locations, radio and cellular transmitter sites, and fiber optic cable routes; and package of land for an electric power plant. The Multifamily segment engages in development, leasing, and long-term ownership of residential rental communities. The Real Estate - Resort/Residential segment engages in land entitlement, planning, pre-construction engineering, stewardship, and conservation activities. The Mineral Resources segment includes oil and gas royalties, rock and aggregate royalties, and royalties from a cement operation leased to National Cement Company of California, Inc.; and the management of water assets and infrastructure projects. The Farming segment farms, produces, and sells wine grapes, almonds, pistachios, hay, and olives. The Ranch Operations segment includes grazing lease and game management, and land maintenance activities, as well as ancillary land uses comprising filming; and guided game hunts. Tejon Ranch Co. was founded in 1843 and is based in Lebec, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew  Walker | President & CEO | Age 54 | Compensation: $914,150 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 65 people. Revenue per employee of $763K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $26K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Tejon Ranch Co is a small-cap industrials business with a $460M market cap on $50M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and -0% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The company is burning through $411,000 of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 8.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 25% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 566% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.660514372163389},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 54/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Tejon Ranch Co (TRC) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Strong Earnings Growth and a ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/tejon-ranch-co-trc-q3-011241243.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794013961.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Tejon Ranch outlines capital-light shift as Hard Rock Casino Tejon breaks ground on 406-room hotel (NYSE:TRC)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668652-tejon-ranch-outlines-capital-light-shift-as-hard-rock-casino-tejon-breaks-ground-on-4